 Omitting `--execute` only emits the compact code/metadata bundle and does not connect. An existing caller namespace or prior local output is refused; failures preserve partial evidence and do not retry. Actual root/cache/restoration/Python pins are from completed prerequisite records, but no successful scientific import or Windows-pickle compatibility is claimed. The root's next action after deployment remains the fixed two interface canaries.
 
 Independent review report fields required by the installer: `source_adoptable: true` and `installer_source_sha256` equal to this exact source. Preparation fixtures are synthetic stdlib metadata checks only and never become root inputs or actual results.
+
+V2 changes only service lifecycle metadata: six project services permit exactly RUNNING/EXITED; sglang permits exactly STOPPED. The fresh actual status of every service must match `protected_services_observed` and belong to its separate allowed list. That actual observation is copied unchanged into queue authorization. An EXITED service is merely a resource fact, not scientific completion. Original v1 and its finding remain untouched.
